<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramanetaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1842</span> · Also known as Abderremane</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramanetaka was a Merina prince and military governor from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> who fled after the death of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radama-i">Radama I</a> and around 1830 seized the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moheli">Moheli</a> (Mwali) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a>. He adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and the name Abderremane and ruled as sultan until his death in 1842, when his young daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/djoumbe-fatima">Djoumbe Fatima</a> succeeded him.</p></div>
